<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ithaca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ithaki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ithaca is a small Ionian island off the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> and the mainland, famed as the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseus">Odysseus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a>. After centuries under Byzantine, Norman and Italian lords it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> around 1500 and shared the history of the Ionian Islands: French rule, the Septinsular Republic, British protection and union with Greece in 1864.</p></div>
